
# Learning in the Fog -- AI on the Edge #####################################

If there is a subject with a greater reliance on impenentrable jargon than
computing, I have yet to find it. Fog? Edge? (Mist, even?) Since "cloud" has
become the accepted term for distributed computing, computation that happens
locally has started to acquire its own terminology building on the same
metaphor. A smart phone or an IoT device is an _edge_ device (a _droplet_
perhaps, or _edge node_). The set of edge devices on a network make a _fog_ or
_mist_.[^rain]

